        <p class="text-secondary max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Every score is computed on the phone. Heart has no server and no account, so your data only goes somewhere if you send it. The formulas are listed below with their sources.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Guarantees panel (terminal style, same idiom as the homepage stack.txt). -->
      <div class="section-reveal rounded-2xl border border-border overflow-hidden mb-12">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 bg-surface border-b border-border" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-error/70"></div>
          <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/70"></div>
          <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-accent/70"></div>
          <span class="ml-2 text-hint text-xs font-mono">heart-privacy.txt</span>
        </div>
        <dl class="bg-bg p-5 md:p-6 font-mono text-xs md:text-sm space-y-3">
          {[
            ['Compute',   'Every score is calculated on the phone.'],
            ['Account',   'None. There is nothing to sign up for.'],
            ['Server',    'None. There is no Heart server to send data to.'],
            ['Telemetry', 'None. No analytics and no ads.'],
            ['Network',   'OpenStreetMap map tiles. Only if you turn them on: Google Drive backup, the Coach model download (~806 MB, from Hugging Face), and phone-to-phone sync over your own Wi-Fi.'],
            ['Backups',   'Written to Download/Heart on the phone, which is kept when Heart is uninstalled. After a reinstall you point Heart at that folder. Anything newer than the last backup is lost.'],
            ['Maths',     'Published formulas, each with its source (list below).'],
          ].map(([k, v]) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
              <dt class="text-hint sm:w-28 shrink-0">{k}</dt>
              <dd class="text-primary/85 flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent hidden sm:inline" aria-hidden="true">→</span>{v}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="section-reveal mb-12">
        <HeartArchitectureDiagram />
      </div>

      <!-- Validation card: the strongest credibility signal, kept visible. -->
      <div class="section-reveal mb-6 p-5 rounded-2xl bg-bg border border-accent/30">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent/15 border border-accent/40 flex items-center justify-center text-base">✓</div>
          <div class="min-w-0 w-full">
            <p class="text-accent text-xs font-mono tracking-widest mb-1.5">VALIDATION · 14 ALGORITHMS · 92 TEST CASES · RUN 2026-09-28</p>
            <p class="text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Each closed-form algorithm in Heart gives the same output as <span class="text-accent">a numpy reference implementation of the same formula</span>, to within <span class="text-accent font-mono">1.42 × 10⁻¹⁴</span>, which is floating-point rounding.
            </p>
            <p class="text-secondary text-xs leading-relaxed">
              The check is a test in the app's repository (<span class="text-primary/70 font-mono text-[11px] break-all">test/algorithm_validation_test.dart</span>); the source isn't public. The formulas come from Tanaka 2001, Uth 2004, Keytel 2005, Holt 1957, ESC/NASPE 1996, Banister 1975 and Coyle 1998.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Deep technical reference behind ONE toggle. -->
      <details class="group section-reveal rounded-2xl border border-border overflow-hidden mb-10">
        <summary class={`flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3.5 bg-surface cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden hover:bg-surface/60 transition-colors ${focusRing}`}>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-error/70"></div>
            <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/70"></div>
            <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-accent/70"></div>
            <span class="ml-2 text-hint text-xs font-mono">formulas-and-references.txt</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs select-none">
            <span class="text-secondary">open this for the formulas</span>
            <span class="text-accent group-open:hidden" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
            <span class="text-accent hidden group-open:inline" aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
          </div>
        </summary>

        <div class="border-t border-border bg-bg px-5 md:px-6 py-6">
          <div class="space-y-2.5 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            {[
              ['HRV',           'RMSSD · ESC/NASPE Task Force · Eur. Heart J. 17:354 · 1996'],
              ['HRmax',         'Age-predicted max · Tanaka et al. · Med. Sci. Sports Exerc. 32:1591 · 2001'],
              ['HR zones',      '5-zone partition · HRmax × [0.60, 0.70, 0.80, 0.90]'],
              ['VO2max',        'Heart-rate ratio method · Uth et al. · Eur. J. Appl. Physiol. 91:111 · 2004'],
              ['Calories',      'HR + age + weight + sex · Keytel et al. · J. Sports Sci. 23:289 · 2005'],
              ['Distance',      'Haversine great-circle · spherical-earth approximation'],
              ['Cardiac drift', 'Early-third vs late-third HR · Coyle framework · 1998'],
              ['Strain',        'TRIMP zone-weighted load · Banister & Calvert · 1975'],
              ['Sleep stages',  'Rule-based 5-min HR-bucket classifier · 4 stages'],
              ['Sleep priors',  'Bayesian post-hoc correction · Sleep-EDF · Kemp et al. 2000'],
              ['Recovery',      'Composite · HRV percentile vs your 30-day baseline'],
              ['Readiness',     'Holt linear exponential smoothing · Holt · ONR memo 52 · 1957'],
              ['Rhythm hint',   '4-feature thresholding · pNN50 + CoV(RR) + RMSSD + RR range'],
              ['Storage',       'SharedPreferences + JSONL · app sandbox · backups in Download/Heart'],
              ['Network',       'OpenStreetMap tiles · opt-in: Google Drive backup, Coach model download, Wi-Fi phone sync'],
              ['Server',        'None'],
            ].map(([key, val]) => (
              <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:gap-4 sm:items-baseline font-mono">
                <span class="text-hint shrink-0 sm:w-32">{key}</span>
                <span class="text-primary/80"><span class="text-accent hidden sm:inline" aria-hidden="true">→ </span>{val}</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <p class="text-hint text-xs text-center max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        The validation above only checks that the <span class="text-secondary">maths</span> is implemented correctly. It says nothing about end-to-end accuracy: sleep staging vs PSG and calories vs calorimetry haven't been independently measured yet.
      </p>
    </div>
